{
  "requirement": "An application supporting tracked source inspection returns `Self::NodeData` for the requested path and selector. The SDK interns that data in the domain's cache to obtain `NodeId<Self>`. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error. The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item. For source identities the application can supply independently, implement `source_address` to recover the project-relative outline address from the domain identity. Other identities return `None`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`.\n\n- **Interning and the returned `NodeId`.**\n  - `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` uses a `TestDomain` whose `source_node` maps `alpha.txt`, `beta.txt` and `visible/selected.txt` to `TestNode` ids 8, 9 and 7. It asserts the recorded dependencies equal `intern_node(TestNode{id:8})`, `id:9` and so on. So the data the application returns is interned into the same `NodeId` the cache hands out.\n  - `project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]` asserts that the domain's `read_nodes` are `[\"source-node\",\"source-node\"]`. It also asserts the dependency is `intern_node(\"source-node\")`.\n- **Unsupported or invalid address returns an error.** The `direct_source_reads…` test passes an unknown path (`unknown.txt`) and an unsupported selector (`line[unknown]`). Both return an \"unsupported source item\" error, leave `dependencies()` empty, and trigger no reads. It also checks that a failure during the read itself (\"prepared source read failed\") is surfaced and records no dependency. `project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[an_unmapped_hit_fails_the_search]` repeats the unmapped-address error through search.\n- **The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item.**\n  - In `project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[agent_node_addresses_round_trip_and_reject_inconsistent_identities_before_reads]`, `list_sources` produces entries with a node id. `read_node` with only `{\"node\":…}` then reads the same source and gets the same dependencies as the path and data forms. This only works if the cache remembered the address.\n  - The same test passes a made-up `node` id (10000) and inconsistent combinations, which are all rejected before any read.\n  - The configured-agent test makes the same check end to end. It reads a mapped node by id and gets the snapshot text, not the on-disk contents.\n- **`source_address` recovers the address, and other identities return `None`.** `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` asserts that `source_address(source_node(&method))` returns `Some(method)`. It asserts `None` for every non-source `HabeasNode` kind (requirement, reference set, selection, definition, site review). It also asserts `None` for a `Source` node with the non-`repo` scheme `generated`. Together these cover a source identity the application can recover and identities it cannot.\n\nThe trait default for `source_address` is a constant `None`. The default for `source_node` returns an error and applies only to applications that don't support source inspection. Neither is a gap, since the requirement targets supporting applications. The `HabeasDomain` non-UTF-8 path error is an unnamed edge case. The mapping-error behaviour it shares with the SDK is tested through the project test domain.\n\nNo gaps found.",
  "references": "1d29a32082b25d649b6110366e39b9fc87deb5e567f66edeb4008297385b5324",
